    "title": "Intermittent CI issue:                                    AssertionError: Unexpected stderr LLVM ERROR: IO failure on output stream: Broken pipe !=",
    "body": "Looks like there are new intermittent CI issues of the form `                                   AssertionError: Unexpected stderr LLVM ERROR: IO failure on output stream: Broken pipe !=`.\n\nNot sure when they started happening? Maybe after https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/36100?\n\nIt could make sense to try to reproduce/bisect and fix this upstream in LLVM and possibly temporarily use llvm 22?\n\nExamples:\n\n* https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/actions/runs/36684426510/job/109787331885?pr=36033#step:11:25384\n* https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/actions/runs/36602839470/job/109524274533?pr=36383#step:11:3974",
